sections.code:
ROSTER NOTATION  -  list the members between braces
  A = {2, 3, 5, 7}
  B = {red, green, blue}
  E = {}                 the empty set, also written ∅

SET-BUILDER NOTATION  -  state the membership rule instead
  A = { x ∈ Z : x is prime and x < 10 }
  read:  the set of integers x such that x is prime and x < 10
  same set as the roster above:  {2, 3, 5, 7}

MEMBERSHIP  -  one question, one yes-or-no answer
  3 ∈ A      true    3 is one of the listed members
  4 ∉ A      true    4 is not listed
  {3} ∈ A    false   A contains the number 3, not the one-element set {3}

ORDER AND REPETITION CARRY NO INFORMATION
  {1, 2, 2, 3} = {3, 2, 1}      both name the same three members
